From b0af01206e55bb91278a04820ef2537cdf9e85e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenATV STB Kodi <noreply@openatv.local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: avoid blocking drain on Dreambox MIPS sink switches

The BCM7435 PCM implementation used by DM7080 and DM820 can block in
snd_pcm_drain() while ActiveAE changes from the GUI stream to a movie stream.
ActiveAE gives the synchronous CONFIGURE request five seconds, so the late
reply leaves its state machine out of sequence and audio packets subsequently
time out or play in short stalled bursts.

The old stream is closed immediately after Drain().  Drop its queued frames
and prepare it instead of waiting in the vendor drain implementation.  This
matches the workaround already proven on the related VuPlus Broadcom PCM path
but is selected separately for Dreambox MIPS builds.
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
index 872def41f1..5f24070e91 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
@@ -991,8 +991,15 @@ void CAESinkALSA::Drain()
   if (!m_pcm)
     return;
 
-  snd_pcm_drain(m_pcm);
-  snd_pcm_prepare(m_pcm);
+  /* Dreambox MIPS vendor PCM may wait indefinitely here.  OpenSink() calls
+   * Drain() synchronously while ActiveAE's CONFIGURE request has a five-second
+   * timeout.  The sink is deinitialized immediately afterwards, so queued
+   * samples do not need to be played to completion. */
+  const int dropResult = snd_pcm_drop(m_pcm);
+  if (dropResult < 0)
+    CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "CAESinkALSA::Drain - snd_pcm_drop returned {} ({})", dropResult,
+              snd_strerror(dropResult));
+  snd_pcm_prepare(m_pcm);
 }
 
 void CAESinkALSA::AppendParams(std::string &device, const std::string &params)
-- 
